Using a throw-helper would be IMO better here.
```c#
if (_currentHeadersStream != null)
{
    ThrowCreateHeadersInterleaved();
}

// ....

// Note: no inlining attributes here!
private void ThrowCreateHeadersInterleaved()
{
    // ...
}
```
So the JIT sees it's a non-returning method and won't inline it and will instead place it on a cold-path. Thus making the happy-path shorter.

The same on the other places.

PS: this could be done in a separate PR (I can look into this later on).
